wo separate bookings instead of one combined booking.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. A $199 flight was available, but it has one stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge in New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**Why there are two bookings:** I first tried to book the flight and hotel together, but the request timed out. Before trying again, I checked Dana's reservations to avoid booking anything twice. The flight had gone through but the hotel hadn't, so I booked the hotel by itself. I checked again afterwards: there's exactly one flight and one hotel booking, with no duplicates.", "type": "text"}]}]}